// Sample notifications for DeClear.
//
// These are fixed example messages a user can try without pasting their own
// text. Each one carries hand-written, deterministic example results — NOT
// generated by any AI model. They are fixed examples authored for the demo so
// the interface can be shown end to end. The real Message_Processor service
// (and real translation) is a later milestone.
//
// IMPORTANT (truthfulness): we only ship predefined outputs for the declared
// combinations below — the three sample messages, in the two declared
// languages (English and French), at the three explanation levels (brief,
// standard, guided). We never pretend to translate or explain arbitrary text.
//
// Result shape matches the Processing_Result contract from the design doc:
// explanation, requiredActions[], importantDates[], urgencyLevel
// ('None' | 'Low' | 'Medium' | 'High'), and uncertaintyIndicators[].
//
// Each sample's `results` is keyed first by language code ('en' | 'fr'), then
// by explanation level ('brief' | 'standard' | 'guided'). The fields that are
// not language/level dependent (dates, urgency) are shared, but we still author
// each variant in full so the output is genuinely different per setting.

export const URGENCY_LEVELS = ['None', 'Low', 'Medium', 'High']

